course: dictionary
lesson: 3647
title: Words that glow
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A firefly is a small flying beetle whose tail glows at night, so the word is not really about fire. Context helps you see this. «Fireflies are beetles that make cold light in their tails» tells you the light is cool, not hot, because the beetle is the thing making the light.
explain: Look at «On a summer evening a field can twinkle with fireflies.» Twinkle and field show you that the fireflies are little lights moving in the dark. Ask yourself what word would fit: sparks? stars? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Some words in a text give you clues about the thing itself. «Each kind has its own flash code» tells you that each kind of firefly blinks in its own pattern. Science writers and story writers both use firefly, but for different reasons, so the words around it change how it feels.
fact: A firefly is a small flying beetle whose tail glows with a soft light.
fact: «Cold light» means light made with almost no heat, like a glow stick.
fact: Scientists call this bioluminescence: a living thing making light inside its body.
fact: «Flash code» means the pattern of blinks that each kind of firefly uses.
fact: Some people use firefly for a glow-worm or any insect that makes its own light.
exercise: «Fireflies are beetles that make cold light in their tails.» What is a firefly? | *A small flying beetle whose tail glows | A dry leaf blown by the wind | A kind of bird that sings at night | A tiny fish that swims in the sea
exercise: «Each kind has its own flash code.» What does flash code mean? | A loud noise made in a field | *The pattern of light flashes that each kind uses | The number of legs on a beetle | A secret password written in a jar
exercise: «A glow stick, a firefly and the northern lights all glow without burning.» What does cold light mean in the lesson sentence «Fireflies... make cold light»? | Dim light that is hard to see | Icy and frozen light | Blue light only | *Light with almost no heat
test: A firefly glows without burning. Why? | It is hidden inside a glass jar | It is wrapped in a warm blanket of leaves | The light comes from the moon | *Its light is made by a chemical reaction in its body, with almost no heat
test: What does bioluminescence mean? | A machine that makes electric lamps | *A living thing making light inside its body | A kind of fire that spreads across a field | A word for a summer evening
exam: Why might a writer choose firefly in a story about a summer night? | It is a word for a loud, angry insect | It is the name of a bird that sings at dawn | *It suggests magic, wonder and warm summer evenings | It means a fire that spreads quickly across a field
